I've got a game mechanics question here... but first a little story to
explain why =p

My Wizard was walking around with a very corroded helmet and gloves,
which at that point offered zero AC protection, so I needed to find
some more. I had just cleared Ft. Ludios, so I had a brilliant idea, I
went and picked up *every* helmet and pair of padded gloves that was
dropped, and with the help of a BoH and the Eye's Branchport, I took
them all to the Minetown altar to B/C/U test. So I pull out the first
batch, drop it on the altar, pick it all up, throw away the cursed
stuff, and begin to wear and remove each and every hat/gloves to check
the enchantment.

Needless to say, it was quirte slow and tedious, so I decided to give
up on that idea, and only test the blessed items, assuming that if it
had any +x enchantment, it would have to be blessed. That made it a
lot quicker, and I got some +1 gloves and +2 helmet for my troubles.
+5 AC for a little trouble is not bad.

So, my question. Is my assumption correct in that all those uncursed
helmets/gloves are +0, or could there be some +5 uncursed glovees in
there I didn't try on? Or did I do the smart thing by only checking
the blessed ones? There were a few blessed +0 items, and thats kinda
making me doubt this, and think they may be independant of each other.



